# Inline meta row (primary + secondary on one line)

When a row shows **avatar/icon + primary label + secondary text** (name + date, title + status, assignee + time):

## Do

- One horizontal flex container: **`tm-inline-meta`** (Task Manager — `admin/src/app/task-manager/styles/_shared.scss`).
- **`tm-inline-meta-primary`** for the main label; **`tm-inline-meta-secondary`** for muted/date/meta.
- **`align-items: center`** on the row; **same `font-size` and `line-height`** on primary and secondary (usually `var(--fs-base)` / `1.5rem`). Muted = color only, not a smaller font.
- Keep avatar in the same flex row, not on a separate line from the name.

```html
<span class="tm-inline-meta">
  <app-tm-avatar [person]="person" [size]="24" />
  <span class="tm-inline-meta-primary">{{ person.name }}</span>
  <span class="tm-inline-meta-secondary">{{ relativeTime(createdAt) }}</span>
</span>
```

## Do not

- Split primary and secondary into **sibling blocks** with different typography utilities (`text-sm` on one only, `font-weight: 600` on name without matching line-height).
- Use **`align-items: baseline`** for name + date on the same row (causes visible vertical drift).
- Rely on **`contains()`** alone on click-outside handlers after the click target node was removed in the same event — use **`event.composedPath()`** for pane dismiss (see task detail panel).

## Reference

- Task detail **Created by**: `task-detail-panel.component.html`
- Comment header meta: `.tm-comment-meta` in `_detail.scss`
